@inherits ErrorBoundaryBase
@* A caught exception renders the marker and nothing else — never the child, and never a half-written
   subtree: Blazor discards the failing tree rather than flushing what it had built, so a renderer
   that throws part-way cannot leak markup onto the page.

   The marker is an element with attributes rather than an HTML comment, because the Razor compiler
   strips comments out of .razor markup before they reach a response. It carries no message: an
   editor reading the page source can see exactly which zone or block failed, and a visitor sees an
   empty span and the rest of the page. *@
@if (CurrentException is null)
{
    @ChildContent
}
else if (ErrorContent is not null)
{
    @ErrorContent(CurrentException)
}
else
{
    <span data-cms-render-failed="@ScopeMarker" data-cms-zone="@ZoneKey" data-cms-block="@BlockId"></span>
}
